# Merge strategy for files this FRAMEWORK repository itself tracks.
#
# This file only governs merges inside the workspace repo. context/ and each
# projects/<group>/<repo>/ are separate git repositories with their own
# .gitattributes — a rule here about a path under either does nothing, because
# git never merges across a repository boundary. context's own merge rules
# live in context/.gitattributes, tracked by that repo.

# .agents/skills/ is fetched output (see .agents/skills.manifest), never
# tracked here, so there is nothing to merge. If skills.lock ever conflicts,
# re-run `ws skills sync` and commit the result rather than hand-merging it.
